{{!
    @template tool_vae/anchor_warning

    The warning a claim carries when the platform no longer says what the claim says; nothing when the anchor holds.

    The template holds no logic. One key is HTML (triple braces): noticehtml, a notification made by the core
    ($output->notification()), whose message names the record escaped by tool_vae\output\anchor_warning.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the warning

    Example context (json):
    {
        "noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-warning alert-block fade in\" role=\"alert\">The record was renamed.</div>"
    }
}}
{{#noticehtml}}{{{noticehtml}}}{{/noticehtml}}
